h-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788946659077839001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eebc5f6e-1f83-4bed-a1c5-df6797541a7b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c437-d221-8471-47a7"},{"link_uuid":"6be4b0f0-84bb-4396-b02e-d2016444521f","relation":"blocks","target_id":"3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"}],"description":"## Symptom\nGerrit change 2888 patch set 1 (359e5b214f99e8a43ffa2c9203fbd4a6aaf97cdc) received Verified -1 in GitHub Actions run 34326885726, job 102386780456, Python 3.12 default suite. Exactly one test failed while 20,176 passed and 82 skipped:\n\n`tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py::test_marker_lock_serializes_posix_access`\n\nExpected event order: `first-has-lock`, `first-done`, `second-done`. Actual order: `first-has-lock`, `second-done`, `first-done`.\n\n## Scope boundary\nThe triggering Gerrit change only condenses comments in `src/rebar/reducer`; do not modify that documentation change to mask this failure and do not retry CI without a proven environmental cause. A separate `/rebar-debug` session owns diagnosis and any behavioral fix.\n\n## Investigation plan\n- Reproduce the ordering failure deterministically from current `origin/main` in a fresh worktree.\n- Establish whether the production marker lock, the test synchronization/oracle, or process scheduling permits the second process to report completion early.\n- Compare passing and failing event traces and test one root-cause hypothesis at a time.\n- Add or strengthen a RED behavioral test at the real lock boundary, implement the smallest class-level fix, and run the focused contention suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic reproduction or equivalent controlled failpoint proves the failure mechanism.\n- [ ] The root cause identifies whether production locking or the test oracle is wrong.\n- [ ] A RED-first regression test fails for the proven reason on the unfixed tree.\n- [ ] The fix preserves marker-lock mutual exclusion and cleanup semantics.\n- [ ] The focused marker/fcntl contention tests pass repeatedly without timing-sleep synchronization.\n- [ ] The fix lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","detected_by":"verified","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","3e32-a859-2153-4a1b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","flaky-test","gerrit","locking"],"ticket_id":"f28d-cc1b-c3e3-45af","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Marker-lock serialization test permits second process to finish before lock holder","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["561dd00c-7e8d-4d1b-9fb4-df65ef1df4ad","eebc5f6e-1f83-4bed-a1c5-df6797541a7b","6be4b0f0-84bb-4396-b02e-d2016444521f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788952201233362001,"uuid":"de5343bd-0a1f-4295-ad67-5098cabb8e94"}